 1 big thing: Next year&#x27;s travel hot spots 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Kayak. Chart: Alex Fitzpatrick/Axios Cities in Guatemala, Morocco and El Salvador are among the 10 highest-trending international destinations for 2027 travel, Alex Fitzpatrick writes from new Kayak data. 

 That's thanks to new hotels and flight routes, travelers' desire to make their money go further, and, in Morocco's case, early interest ahead of the 2030 World Cup. 💸 Kayak's Kayla DeLoache tells Axios of the top-10 list: "The average flight price might be high for some of these destinations ... but when you get there, your dollar stretches further. You can get some really great hotel nightly rates."

 How it works: Kayak's data is based on U.S. searches made between April 1 and Sept. 25 of this year for travel any time next year, compared to the same period a year prior.

 These "trending" destinations had the biggest bumps in search interest. Zoom out: Tokyo, Cancún and London are Kayak's most-searched foreign cities overall for travel in 2027.

 😎 Between the lines: Expedia says 2027 will be the year of "Un-Adulting," with travelers looking to "escape from adult responsibilities and go on carefree vacations full of childlike joy." 

 It's also seeing a rise in one-night stays — what it's calling "trip snacking." What's next: Kayak and similar platforms have been rolling out new AI features designed to help travelers plan their trips using both old-school search and new natural-language options.

