 2. 🤖 Doctors vs. AI 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images Doctors who disagree with AI could be in greater danger of losing a malpractice suit, Axios' Adriel Bettelheim reports from a new study. 

 In simulated court cases, researchers found that mock juries were more likely to side with plaintiffs in malpractice suits when AI disagreed with radiologists. 🧠 One scenario involved a brain bleed on a CT scan that resulted in irreversible brain damage.

 When AI flagged the condition but the radiologist didn't think there was a problem, the jurors sided with the plaintiff nearly 75% of the time, the researchers wrote in NEJM AI . Yes, but: A smaller share of jurors ruled against the physician when they were told about the AI system's error rate.

