 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Shoppers pour into Macy's Herald Square in New York this morning. Photo: Adam Gray/AP 🛒 We're still doing that Black Friday thing: Despite weeks of online deals, people lined up before sunrise at the flagship Macy's Herald Square in Manhattan, with some filming on their phones as they burst in. Sensormatic, which tracks retail foot traffic, says Black Friday continues to draw more store visits than any other day. Keep reading . 📚 Former President Biden's " Promise Me, America " sold around 21,000 copies during its debut week, according to Circana, which tracks about 85% of hardcover sales. The book hit No. 1 on The New York Times hardcover nonfiction bestseller list but didn't approach the sales of memoirs by Barack Obama and Bill Clinton. More from AP . 💻 Hackers breached the Air Force's flagship cloud computing platform, which could jeopardize sensitive tactical, personnel and logistics data, Reuters reports. The intrusion at Cloud One was ‌discovered within the past month or so during upgrade work. The Air Force said it "does not comment on the ​security posture, vulnerabilities or operational status of specific networks and systems." Keep reading . 
 
