 4. 🚁 1 for the road: Drones find lost pets 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Maura Losch/Axios Some pet owners are turning to drones to find their lost animals, Axios Dallas' Ned Oliver reports. 

 📈 Demand for drone searches took off this year, says Drew Smith of Overhead Perspectives in Weatherford, Texas.

 His drones use thermal cameras to pick up an animal's heat signature from above, covering hundreds of acres far faster than a search on foot. 🐶 Smith recalls one woman whose two dogs had been gone for about 25 hours in a heavily wooded area. "Within five minutes, I'd located the dogs," he says.

 He's also searched for cats and, once, a calf that got something stuck on its head and wandered into dense brush. Go deeper ... Get Axios Local . 

 
 
